  "review_notes": [
    "Reviewed the current top-level proposal, not the different proposal embedded in context.prior_result. Read proposal.json lines 1\u2013127, functionality.md lines 1\u201337, fact-dispositions.json lines 1\u2013377, and link-dispositions.json lines 1\u2013321.",
    "All five proposed writes concern owned subjects and are supported. The two type writes replace unsupported ownership assertions with local borrowed-pointer contracts. The physics and TU state writes correctly bound latch lifetime and distinguish duration exhaustion from continuation failure. The collision write correctly describes synchronous conditional callback invocation and guarded landing-lag use.",
    "Independently checked the selector and common entry implementation, Float continuation and return helper, active Peach motion table, common and Peach motion enums, Peach field declarations, aerial-jump delegate, collision wrapper, and landing switch. Directional mapping follows active selector/table behavior plus enum arithmetic, not rendered names.",
    "The unsigned gate admits selector IDs 65 and 66, excluding adjacent 64 and 67. Item access is short-circuited and null-guarded. Entry queries the selector again. IASA continuation bookkeeping precedes interrupt arbitration, and chained entry can clear the latch in that same invocation.",
    "The functionality document appropriately limits exceptional floating-point discussion to source-level interpretation and leaves runtime reachability and compiled behavior unproved. Duration is a float; subtraction is not saturating. Neither timer exhaustion nor reasserted continuation input directly changes the release latch.",
    "The landing callback is not retained by ft_80082C74. FloatAttack motions match none of the ordinary aerial landing cases, so both command-flag branches reach basic landing without reading the uninitialized lag local or executing lag division/conversion.",
    "The artifact ledger marks the existing collision data_flow fact retain, although the current proposal writes a refined value for that same subject/type. My independent disposition below is supersede to reflect that supported refinement. This does not require changing the proposal.",
    "Retained latch descriptions are interpreted as descriptions of the current attack entry, not a fighter-wide irreversible condition. Their stronger interpretation is explicitly deferred below. No additional corrective write is required beyond the supplied physics and TU refinements.",
    "No replacement proposal, new relation, entity, merge, or shared-artifact mutation was produced."
  ],
